Z||000018||JSocha||12-21-2001||03:25 PM||||Thanks guys.  You had inadvertently given me some leads with your posts...and I'm going to have to check my computer at home now.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> How many fricken times can one "UNINSTALL" that stupid fricken "Gator" program?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I swear I have uninstalled it so many cotton pickin times now and somehow it gets reinstalled...fricken computer fairy?<P>Just got done UNINSTALLING it again and going through MSCONFIG to make sure there were no settings activating GATOR.  It doesn't show up in my control panel INSTALL/UNINSTALL screen anymore.  For how long though is my next question.  I hate that program, let alone never wanted it installed in the first place.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>And somehow I have YAHOO Messanger on my computer as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  How did that get installed...I don't use YAHOO nor do I know anybody "officially" on it to use it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Not as many POP-UPS occuring, but still happening.||||reg||8
Z||000019||TRiAD||12-21-2001||03:35 PM||||Programs like Gator are essentially designed like a worm. They are self-executing and have SEVERAL "start" indicators, throughout the machine. There's a company that does browser skins who's program is identical. <P>These could be the source of your problem, as their programs occasionally are set as an invisible "bot", looking for pop-up ads, and registring you on them. (PIV only). <P>Anyway, your ISP could also be doing this, or selling your info to people who use pop-ups. <P>You no longer need to go to a website that uses pop-ups to get popped. They can find you on the net via your IP or other info (again PIV only on the "other" info). <P>Ads suck.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
