Z||000028||DRH||12-21-2001||06:40 PM||||One place programs like to hide their startup is in the registry. From Start &gt; Run type in regedit (Not sure if it's same for all denominations of Windows). Navigate the folders to:  <P>HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run<P>Anything listed there will be run when you start the PC. If it looks suspicious (like ...\gator.exe for example), write down EXACTLY what it says, then delete it. Reboot and see if it's gone. If you accidently delete something you wanted you can add it back by adding a new string value with regedit. Windows shouldn't HAVE to have anything in there to run, but deleting the wrong thing may make a virus checker or something not start. A lot of things that show up as the small icons next to your clock in the lower right of the screen get started from here.<BR>||||reg||1
